---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import InfoPage from "../props/InfoPage.astro";
const content = [
  {
    title: "About TeckPac",
    page_content: [
      "TeckPac is a technical consulting firm focused exclusively on solving the real-world challenges of food and beverage packaging. Led by industry expert Piaras de Cleir, the company brings over 25 years of experience working across bottles, closures, materials, and manufacturing systems. From early-stage development to troubleshooting issues in market, TeckPac supports clients at every stage of the packaging lifecycle.",
      "What sets TeckPac apart is a deeply technical, hands-on approach. Rather than relying on assumptions, every engagement is grounded in detailed investigation—evaluating material selection, part design, manufacturing conditions, and system interactions. This approach has helped uncover and resolve complex issues such as carbonation loss in soft drink bottles caused by subtle preform defects, as well as widespread cracking in beverage closures driven by changes in materials and processing conditions. By identifying root causes—not just symptoms—TeckPac delivers solutions that are both effective and sustainable.",
      "Beyond troubleshooting, TeckPac has a strong track record in packaging development and commercialization. The company has helped clients move from concept to market in compressed timelines by leveraging existing assets and optimizing design for manufacturability. In one case, a new beverage package was successfully developed and launched in just five months, reducing capital investment while accelerating speed to market.",
      "TeckPac’s expertise spans a wide range of packaging formats and technologies, including injection and compression molded closures, blow-molded and injection stretch blow-molded bottles, thermoformed cups and tubs, and sealing technologies such as heat seal and ultrasonic systems. The firm also supports initiatives in lightweighting, sustainability, and material transitions across resins like PET, HDPE, and PP. In addition to consulting, TeckPac offers one of the most comprehensive closure training programs in the industry. These sessions cover everything from the fundamentals of materials and design to advanced topics like manufacturing defects, capping systems, and performance testing. Designed for both experienced professionals and those new to packaging, the training can be tailored to specific teams and delivered on-site or online.",
      "At its core, TeckPac exists to help companies solve problems faster, make better technical decisions, and bring stronger packaging solutions to market. Whether addressing a persistent quality issue, optimizing an existing system, or developing something entirely new, TeckPac provides the expertise and insight needed to get it right.",
    ],
    text_block_title: "More Info",
    page_content_grid: [
      {
        title: "Who We Are",
        items: [
          "Technical consulting firm focused on food & beverage packaging",
          "25+ years of industry experience across bottles, closures, and materials",
          "Led by hands-on packaging expert with deep manufacturing knowledge",
          "Support spans concept development through in-market troubleshooting",
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "What We Do",
        items: [
          "Solve real-world packaging failures and performance issues",
